#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534132} :activity/id #uuid "abd7f8c6-92bf-58ba-8f77-35b892e03ec2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050299 :topic/id #uuid "3d9b9134-f2c7-559d-b631-25a1da8ede8d" :topic/math-academy-id 338} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534120 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd85c349-b07a-5ce7-acbe-71dec6f51725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320020}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320020} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1395fe-90e5-58b0-b928-c57e2255472b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "42ce6d45-7dcd-53d8-be85-5db5b0c5d792" :question/math-academy-id "q-352247" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}=3{x}^{2}-4x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{1}^{3}]-2[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}]+[2-1] \\\\  & =7\\cdot 1-2(3)+1 \\\\  & =7-6+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "493b3de4-1cb9-5807-ae21-3adf761e5283" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534148}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534132 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42e6b1e1-c481-5131-aa9b-e51fd0e84f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-4x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488608} {:answer/id #uuid "4a697176-e9f1-5136-bc2c-f4d7b21c4c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488616} {:answer/id #uuid "62d7902c-29ca-5bc3-8e15-8a29b24dccf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488659} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9d1eb3-ac76-5c9d-9822-7053bfb20d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488844} {:answer/id #uuid "e00dd37b-1e6f-5de4-8259-64c1940bd61a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-17x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488936}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488616} :answer-field/id #uuid "943cb8b2-64c1-553e-80f2-f883b3ab8a15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ea9dfa89-06eb-5760-a821-cda00c20e204" :question/math-academy-id "q-49458" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-17x+4}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $4$ | $-17$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $16$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-17x+4}{x-4}=4x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-17x+4}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6b313935-bcb5-5009-bac0-2daf40e6de4d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534136}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534136 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f5b864f-ab9e-5526-a0c2-c02feff7679e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}+10\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533328} {:answer/id #uuid "528bf807-f7c8-5d89-ae8b-52082e42ff70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533336} {:answer/id #uuid "96be4dfe-e4e2-5571-943a-fa6959f16012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533505} {:answer/id #uuid "ad15a888-28a0-51eb-b31c-7a799c730314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533555} {:answer/id #uuid "de9a1ad2-05e9-52eb-a0d5-b42eb5191ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533686}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533686} :answer-field/id #uuid "2077670f-b2d2-5635-90e0-1a5bc69c2121" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c9d6ed6b-fbf8-57c0-b691-2915931ac208" :question/math-academy-id "q-114886" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+x-1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 & 4 & 10 \\\\  & 1 & 2 & 5 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+x-1}{x-2}={x}^{2}+2x+5+\\frac{9}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+x-1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+2x+5+\\frac{9}{x-2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x+9{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+5x\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-{0}^{3})+({1}^{2}+{0}^{2})+5(1-0)+9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0-2|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+1+5+9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+6-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8c494919-3b9e-595f-a17c-ad5906d7c222" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534159}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534148 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "287ac481-01e4-501d-92a0-d611e24907eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533240}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533240} :answer-field/id #uuid "123c7483-9bc5-51d0-9fff-02d7158c75ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b15dd44d-79f8-5979-b1d9-ef4007b4896c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533567}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533567} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a416796-2530-56e2-9658-fd2726d65c72" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9e3082ec-c2a4-52d5-af74-aff0c23f65d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-358839" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-3}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{23}{25}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $5$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-3}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-3}{5(x+1/5)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-3}{(x+1/5)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{5}$ | $8$ | $-3$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{8}{5}$ |\n|  | $8$ | $-\\frac{23}{5}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-3}{(x+1/5)} & =8-\\frac{(23/5)}{(x+1/5)} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{23}{5x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-3}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8-\\frac{23}{5x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[8{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-23{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{[8x-\\frac{23}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[8(1-0)-\\frac{23}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[8-\\frac{23\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{5}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{23}{25}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c20a359b-fc4b-5f35-97e3-15ab5d7d2b17"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534159 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9826cc-221a-58f0-a949-003259d10830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247516} {:answer/id #uuid "1935d4e4-d30d-5335-ab50-3b3fa04366e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247651} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9aeadf-fded-5a2b-861d-58af4c73c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247959} {:answer/id #uuid "54ac800d-c455-530d-b963-3aea2be7c145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248185} {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3226bde-c895-54e8-98cf-b5b2df79f6fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "462b058c-0216-5b9a-aa39-6bb6d7bc768e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114896" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3})}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-(-\\frac{1}{12}))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(-\\frac{1}{12})+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(\\frac{1}{12})+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fa2397e7-9076-5f64-a56a-0ac0b05bc47d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534120}}] :activity/title "Integrating Functions Using Polynomial Division" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533127}]}
